{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>At the end of seven years.</b> One might think seven years for each and every loan — Scripture says, ״the seventh year draws near.״ And if you say seven years for each and every loan, for the loans of each and every person — how is it ״drawing near״? You have thus learned: seven years by the count of the shemittah cycle (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:06.299893083Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}